FILE: app/src/fly-controls.ts
```ts
import type { FreeCamera, SceneContext } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { attachConfigurableFreeControl } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function attachFlyControls(
  camera: FreeCamera,
  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,
  scene: SceneContext
): () => void {
  return attachConfigurableFreeControl(camera, canvas, scene, {
    upKeys: ["Space"],
    downKeys: ["PageDown"],
    fastKeys: ["ShiftLeft", "ShiftRight"],
    fastMultiplier: 3,
  });
}
```

I created `src/fly-controls.ts` to delegate to the library’s configurable free-camera control with Space/PageDown vertical keys, both Shift keys as the 3x fast key, and the library’s disposer returned so nothing extra remains active. I’m assuming `attachConfigurableFreeControl` is exported from the package root and that its key options use `KeyboardEvent.code` values, since I couldn’t inspect the runtime library.
